WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Kelly] So, have you
met anybody here yet?

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.528
- [Wiz] Um, no not yet.

00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:04.429
- This is the first time?

00:00:04.429 --> 00:00:05.262
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:06.095
- Okay, they were all excited,

00:00:06.095 --> 00:00:07.109
they were like, "Is he going to perform?"

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:08.149
I'm like, "No, he's actually going to

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:08.982
do something else, so I'm very excited

00:00:08.982 --> 00:00:09.961
about it."

00:00:09.961 --> 00:00:10.989
- Yeah, [Laughs] Sorry.

00:00:10.989 --> 00:00:11.822
- But, you know I'm
obsessed with your son,

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:13.690
I told you backstage I
think he is adorable,

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.930
Sebastian's six now right?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:15.763
- Yeah, he's six years old.

00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:16.688
- Does he rap?

00:00:16.688 --> 00:00:18.940
- He does, he's got like
his own little playlist

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.670
of music, like when I come in the car,

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.380
or when he gets in the car after school,

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.230
he's like, "Daddy play
this song, this song,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.063
that song."

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:26.030
- [Laughs] My daughter's
bossy like that too.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.180
- Yeah, I mean I try to
put him onto new stuff,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.619
and he don't even want to hear it.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:30.658
[Laughter]

00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:32.060
- My daughter, yeah,
she'll try and do that,

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.730
and I'm like, "I love,"
I mean I just grew up

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.610
on Tupac, Ludacris, I love all that stuff,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.443
and anytime it plays she's like,

00:00:36.443 --> 00:00:37.333
"No, I wanna hear this," and I'm like,

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:38.910
"Oh, okay."

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.860
- Oh yeah, for sure, exactly.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.720
- So I heard you also
coach Bastian's is it

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.553
baseball team?

00:00:42.553 --> 00:00:43.650
- I do coach his baseball team, yeah.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.328
- Yeah, that's- I mean-

00:00:45.328 --> 00:00:47.995
[Wiz Laughs] [Audience Applause]

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:52.910
- We have kids in sports,
and I'm just wondering

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.150
what it's like when you show up,

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.440
and you're the coach, and all the parents

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.360
are like, "What?!"

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.050
- Well first it smells a little funny

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:01.883
when I show up.

00:01:01.883 --> 00:01:02.716
- It does, yeah?

00:01:02.716 --> 00:01:03.609
[Laughter]

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.356
- It's like hanging
out with Willie Nelson?

00:01:06.356 --> 00:01:07.189
[Laughter]

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:08.460
- But, um, it's crazy
because one of the coaches

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.280
actually came up to me, he's a fireman,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.750
and he just told me this yesterday,

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.110
he was like, "I was watching TV and I

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.030
seen an interview with you on there,"

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.560
and I was like, "Well what the heck is the

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.730
Dodger's coach doing on TV?"

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.686
He didn't even know I was a rapper, so-

00:01:22.686 --> 00:01:23.640
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.100
- They had to tell him who I was.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.677
- He is seriously out of touch, okay.

00:01:26.677 --> 00:01:28.790
- But it's cool because I felt like maybe

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.630
I'm doing such a good job as a coach,

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.166
he don't know I'm a rapper, so.

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:34.465
- That's really cool though, because

00:01:34.465 --> 00:01:36.886
I feel like as parents it's hard to like

00:01:36.886 --> 00:01:39.680
One, either find something
in common sometimes,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.620
and also just have the
time to do something

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.623
like that, so it's
awesome you take the time

00:01:43.623 --> 00:01:44.456
to do that.

00:01:44.456 --> 00:01:46.204
- Yeah, yeah, for me it's super important.

00:01:46.204 --> 00:01:47.037
I love children, and this is the most

00:01:47.037 --> 00:01:49.206
important time in his life, especially

00:01:49.206 --> 00:01:50.190
spending it with me and his friends

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.760
and the relationships that
they're going to build,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.150
so, any hand that I can have in that,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.420
I'm trying to do it.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.820
- You're a good daddy, yeah.

